{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"15048f956c8acb30","name":"card_unit_m6","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BloodIron/units/card_unit_m6","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"M6","text":"Your HQ takes 1 less damage for each of your units with 4 or more attack.","flavorText":"The Heavy Tank M6 was an American heavy tank developed during WWII, intended to provide the U.S. Army with a powerful, heavily armored vehicle capable of countering German tanks. Designed in 1940, the M6 featured thick armor and was armed with a 76 mm M7 gun and a 37 mm M6 gun in a single turret, along with multiple machine guns. It was one of the largest tanks produced by the United States at the time, weighing over 60 tons. Despite its impressive firepower and armor, the M6 faced significant drawbacks. Its large size and weight made it difficult to transport and maneuver, and by the time it was ready for production, U.S. military doctrine had shifted to prioritize medium tanks, like the M4 Sherman, which were more versatile, more reliable, cheaper, and much easier to transport. As a result, the M6 never saw combat, and only around 40 tanks were produced before the program was canceled in 1944.","faction":"USA","type":"tank","rarity":"Unique","cost":7,"operationCost":3,"attack":7,"defense":7},"defaults":{"Name":"card_unit_m6","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m6_title","SourceString":"M6","LocalizedString":"M6"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":7,"defense":7,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m6_text","SourceString":"Your HQ takes 1 less damage for each of your units with 4 or more attack.","LocalizedString":"Your HQ takes 1 less damage for each of your units with 4 or more attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_m6_history","SourceString":"The Heavy Tank M6 was an American heavy tank developed during WWII, intended to provide the U.S. Army with a powerful, heavily armored vehicle capable of countering German tanks. Designed in 1940, the M6 featured thick armor and was armed with a 76 mm M7 gun and a 37 mm M6 gun in a single turret, along with multiple machine guns. It was one of the largest tanks produced by the United States at the time, weighing over 60 tons. Despite its impressive firepower and armor, the M6 faced significant drawbacks. Its large size and weight made it difficult to transport and maneuver, and by the time it was ready for production, U.S. military doctrine had shifted to prioritize medium tanks, like the M4 Sherman, which were more versatile, more reliable, cheaper, and much easier to transport. As a result, the M6 never saw combat, and only around 40 tanks were produced before the program was canceled in 1944.","LocalizedString":"The Heavy Tank M6 was an American heavy tank developed during WWII, intended to provide the U.S. Army with a powerful, heavily armored vehicle capable of countering German tanks. Designed in 1940, the M6 featured thick armor and was armed with a 76 mm M7 gun and a 37 mm M6 gun in a single turret, along with multiple machine guns. It was one of the largest tanks produced by the United States at the time, weighing over 60 tons. Despite its impressive firepower and armor, the M6 faced significant drawbacks. Its large size and weight made it difficult to transport and maneuver, and by the time it was ready for production, U.S. military doctrine had shifted to prioritize medium tanks, like the M4 Sherman, which were more versatile, more reliable, cheaper, and much easier to transport. As a result, the M6 never saw combat, and only around 40 tanks were produced before the program was canceled in 1944."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamageAddDamage","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamageAddDamageAfterCalc"],"heavyArmo